  </question>
  <question type="multichoice">
    <name>
      <text>MCR_U05_L05_Q04</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p><strong>Question ID:</strong> MCR_U05_L05_Q04</p><p><strong>MLA Standard:</strong> MLA.MCR.PR.7</p><p>Five students are available and two are chosen for the same committee. How many groups are possible?</p>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <defaultgrade>1.0000000</defaultgrade>
    <penalty>0.3333333</penalty>
    <hidden>0</hidden>
    <single>true</single>
    <shuffleanswers>true</shuffleanswers>
    <answernumbering>abc</answernumbering>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[20]]></text>
      <feedback format="html">
        <text><![CDATA[This counts ordered positions, but the committee roles are the same.]]></text>
      </feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[25]]></text>
      <feedback format="html">
        <text><![CDATA[This allows repeated students and counts order.]]></text>
      </feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[5]]></text>
      <feedback format="html">
        <text><![CDATA[This counts individual students, not pairs.]]></text>
      </feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="100" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[10]]></text>
      <feedback format="html">
        <text><![CDATA[Correct. There are 20 ordered pairs, and each group is counted twice, so 10 groups.]]></text>
      </feedback>
    </answer>
  </question>
  <question type="multichoice">
    <name>
      <text>MCR_U05_L05_Q05</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p><strong>Question ID:</strong> MCR_U05_L05_Q05</p><p><strong>MLA Standard:</strong> MLA.MCR.PR.6</p><p>A code has 3 letters followed by 4 digits, with choices already limited to 3 letter symbols and 4 digit symbols for each position. How many one-letter-one-digit codes are possible?</p>]]></text>
